    "lien_position": "1 = first mortgage; 2 or higher = subordinate (B-note, second, mezzanine). Senior loans are repaid first from refinance, sale or liquidation, and a junior loan's NAIC CM category is one notch worse. Blank = 1.",
    "lo_acquisition_costs_pct": "Low end of the range for Acquisition Costs, in percent like the base value. With High, a property's Quality (1-5) positions the value: 3 = base, 5 = the favorable end (see Quality directions). Enter both or neither.",
    "lo_capital_reserves_per_sf": "Low end of the range for Capital Reserves $/SF (SF properties), in dollars like the base value. With High, a property's Quality (1-5) positions the value: 3 = base, 5 = the favorable end (see Quality directions). Enter both or neither.",
